post_install() {
  cat <<'EOF'
smcfan is built by DKMS for every installed kernel 7.3 and newer. Older kernels
still ship the applesmc driver, and their macsmc.h has no SMC key ioctl ABI, so
DKMS skips them on purpose. If you boot both kinds of kernel, expect one
"WARNING: ... exited 77" line per old kernel on install; that is the skip, not a
failure.

The module is not loaded at boot by modules-load.d, because that file applies to
every kernel. mbpfan.service loads it with a leading "-", so it starts cleanly
even where the shim does not exist. To load it by hand:
  sudo modprobe smcfan

Check it:
  lsmod | grep smcfan
  ls -l /dev/smcfan
EOF
}

post_upgrade() {
  post_install
}
